CULTER :
-------------------->
A MongoDB Cluster is a group of MongoDB servers (called nodes) working together to handle large amounts of data .


..> And provide high availability and reliability. Instead of having just one server holding all your data, a cluster distributes the data across multiple servers.

Why is a MongoDB Cluster Used?

..> Scalability:

Scaling means handling more data and traffic without slowing down the system.
.> A cluster allows MongoDB to split the data across multiple servers, so it can handle more data and users. When your data grows, you can add more servers to the cluster.

.> High Availability:

If one server in the cluster fails, other servers can take over, ensuring your database remains available.

.> This is called replication. MongoDB keeps multiple copies of data across different servers in the cluster to make sure the system keeps running even if one server goes down.

Types of Clusters in MongoDB:
-------------------------------->
Sharded Cluster:

Used to handle very large datasets by splitting the data across multiple servers (called shards).

.> MongoDB decides which data goes to which server based on a shard key.


Replica Set:

.> A group of servers that maintain the same data, ensuring that if one server goes down, another server can take over.



















